01:42:41.500 --> 01:42:47.700
Now, what's the point of all this in terms
of looking at analyst ratings?

01:42:48.540 --> 01:42:50.100
What's the point of this example?

01:42:50.620 --> 01:42:51.700
What's the point of all of it?

01:42:51.700 --> 01:43:02.980
Well, the point is, is that as traders,
what we like to see is that we like to see
room for changes in recommendations.

01:43:03.940 --> 01:43:12.580
So in our example, in Abercrombie & Fitch,
six months ago, the landscape will have
looked very, very different.

01:43:12.580 --> 01:43:33.460
The average rating would have been around
a hold to underperform ratings, which
means that there was actually, at the
time, room for upgrades, which in
themselves are catalysts that can get the
stock moving.

01:43:34.820 --> 01:43:51.380
So if you think of an extreme example,
where every single analyst in the market
has a sell recommendation or underperform
recommendation for their rating, what does
that actually mean?

01:43:51.940 --> 01:43:56.560
Well, it actually means that no one can
downgrade the stock.

01:43:56.560 --> 01:44:04.020
No one can downgrade their rating because
every analyst in the market has the lowest
rating possible.

01:44:04.760 --> 01:44:11.780
What can only happen in that situation is
that analysts can upgrade their rating.

01:44:12.100 --> 01:44:14.140
That's the only thing that can happen.

01:44:15.240 --> 01:44:18.000
And of course, it's the same situation in
the opposite.

01:44:18.160 --> 01:44:29.860
If every single analyst has a strong buy
or buy rating on a stock in the market, no
analyst can actually upgrade their rating
in the future.

01:44:30.760 --> 01:44:35.680
In that situation, the only thing that
analysts can do is downgrade their rating.

01:44:35.680 --> 01:44:44.080
And this is why we look at the
distribution of ratings for research
analysts.

01:44:44.080 --> 01:44:51.100
Because in our qualitative analysis, as
traders, we like catalysts.

01:44:51.100 --> 01:44:56.380
We like as many catalysts as possible that
are going to get the stock moving.

01:44:56.980 --> 01:45:12.000
And although it's not a prerequisite or an
absolute necessity for it to be there,
it's always nice to see that for our
potential long ideas, we have room for
upgrades.

01:45:12.000 --> 01:45:30.600
This, however, doesn't mean that when
we're going through our qualitative
analysis, that if we see all analysts with
a buy rating for a potential long idea,

01:45:30.600 --> 01:45:48.700
or we see all analysts with a potential
short idea that we can't actually go long
or short, we just have to be very careful
to understand that in those situations, we
might be entering consensus positioning.

01:45:48.880 --> 01:46:01.720
So we have to be cautious, but by going
through this process, going through this
part of the qualitative process, what
we're actually doing here is understanding
the lay of the land.

01:46:01.720 --> 01:46:16.320
So we're understanding whether there is
actually room for upgrades or downgrades,
and potentially whether there's extreme
bullish or bearish analyst estimates,
ratings, and therefore sentiment.

01:46:17.600 --> 01:46:28.740
When we do have room for upgrades or
downgrades, so when we have room for
upgrades for long ideas, on the upside
with longs,

01:46:28.740 --> 01:46:46.120
It means analysts, on the whole are being
too cautious, and when we have room for
ratings changes to the downside for
potential short ideas, it usually means
that the analysts in the market are in
denial.

01:46:47.500 --> 01:46:54.020
Either way, although it's not a must-have,
we do like to see this.

01:46:54.020 --> 01:47:03.620
We do like to see, as traders, that we
have potential room for upgrades or
downgrades in the way that we're trading.

01:47:04.340 --> 01:47:10.640
Why? Because it means analysts are
responding and not actually predicting
like us.

01:47:11.140 --> 01:47:25.420
We are taking the position, we are
predicting what's going to happen in the
future, and then analysts are responding
to it, and then providing us with
catalysts, and the stock price is moving
on those catalysts.

01:47:26.080 --> 01:47:34.660
What you have to understand about research
analysts is that they are career-driven
corporate salarymen.

01:47:34.660 --> 01:47:42.680
Again, they are career animals, and they
very rarely stick their neck out and make
a big call.

01:47:43.180 --> 01:47:47.880
They just want to get paid, and they just
want to put their kids through private
school.

01:47:49.040 --> 01:48:05.180
Now, of course, we don't go out there and
look for situations to generate trade
ideas where we see stocks that have all
sell ratings and all buy ratings and go
against the analysts.

01:48:05.520 --> 01:48:06.640
That's just ridiculous.

01:48:06.820 --> 01:48:07.440
Of course not.

01:48:07.860 --> 01:48:10.080
You have to go through your processes
properly.

01:48:10.480 --> 01:48:19.060
You identify your positive and negative
outliers, and then you go on to the
qualitative analysis, and this is one part
of it.

01:48:19.060 --> 01:48:38.920
This is one part of it, guys, where you're
understanding the distribution of ratings,
you're understanding the range of
estimates, and you're understanding the
positive or negative skew from the market
when we look at mean consensus estimates
versus midpoints.

01:48:39.920 --> 01:48:48.200
We don't use one part of our trade idea
generation process in isolation to
generate trade ideas.

01:48:48.200 --> 01:48:57.320
We obviously use all of the entire pro
trader systematic process, and this is
just a small part of it.

01:48:57.920 --> 01:48:59.400
We don't use one part of it.

01:48:59.400 --> 01:49:03.200
We don't use one part of it.

01:49:03.200 --> 01:49:04.200
We don't use one part of it.

01:49:04.200 --> 01:49:05.920
We don't use one part of it.

01:49:05.920 --> 01:49:06.200
We don't use one part of it.

01:49:06.200 --> 01:49:07.200
We don't use one part of it.

01:49:07.200 --> 01:49:08.200
We don't use one part of it.

01:49:08.200 --> 01:49:10.200
We don't use one part of it.

01:49:10.200 --> 01:49:11.200
We don't use one part of it.

01:49:11.200 --> 01:49:12.200
We don't use one part of it.

01:49:12.200 --> 01:49:13.280
We don't use one part of it.

01:49:13.280 --> 01:49:14.200
We don't use one part of it.

01:49:14.200 --> 01:49:15.200
We don't use one part of it.

01:49:15.200 --> 01:49:16.200
We don't use one part of it.

01:49:16.200 --> 01:49:17.200
We don't use one part of it.

01:49:17.200 --> 01:49:18.200
We don't use one part of it.

01:49:18.200 --> 01:49:20.200
We don't use one part of it.

